# Cloudflare Pages headers — static security headers.
#
# ── WHERE THE CSP WENT (Dr. Insane RE-GATE R2, blocker B3) ────────────────────
# The Content-Security-Policy is NO LONGER SET HERE. It moved to
# functions/_middleware.js, which issues a fresh per-request nonce and stamps it
# onto every inline <script> as the HTML streams out.
#
# It had to move because this file is static and a nonce is per-request. The old
# policy carried script-src 'unsafe-inline', which made the CSP decorative against
# XSS on pages that hold caller PII — the whole point of having one here.
#
# Do NOT add a Content-Security-Policy line back to this file. Two policies means
# the browser enforces both intersected, so a stale 'unsafe-inline' left here
# would not widen the live policy, but it WOULD make the effective policy
# impossible to reason about from either file alone. One owner, in the middleware.
#
# Everything below is genuinely static and stays here.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  # X-Frame-Options is NOT set here. Framing is owned by functions/_middleware.js,
  # which emits frame-ancestors and X-Frame-Options together so the two can never
  # disagree. It formerly stayed permissive to let the vendor concierge shell iframe
  # this site; that shell is gone and the policy is now 'self' unconditionally.
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(), camera=()

# CSS is no-cache during active development so style fixes actually reach users
# (immutable year-long caching meant edits never propagated). Before go-live,
# version the asset filenames (main.[hash].css) and restore immutable caching.
/css/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/js/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/webfonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
